    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Odometer Verification:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The mileage displayed on the motorcycle’s odometer is recorded. This figure must match the mileage recorded on the logistic receipt (LR) bilty issued at pickup. If the numbers diverge, the carrier must investigate the cause and document any adjustments.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Signed Condition Sign‑Off:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Both parties sign a condition sheet that lists all inspected items and confirms the mileage match. The sign‑off is then attached to the delivery manifest and retained by the carrier for audit purposes.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>Each step is performed in the presence of the recipient to avoid disputes later. The daylight inspection is preferable because natural lighting reduces the risk of missing subtle defects that could be masked by artificial lights. By referencing the pickup photos, the carrier can demonstrate that the vehicle’s exterior has not been altered.</p>

<p>Odometer verification is critical for billing accuracy. The LR bilty, which contains the original mileage at dispatch, acts as the benchmark. A mismatch triggers a mileage audit, which may involve re‑checking the vehicle’s internal mileage logs or consulting the manufacturer’s service records.</p>

<p>Finally, the signed condition sign‑off serves as a legal acknowledgment that the vehicle was delivered in the same condition and mileage as it was sent. This document protects both the carrier and the customer, providing a clear trail of responsibility and ensuring that any future claims can be resolved swiftly.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



